# Deployment Guide

This Hexo blog is configured to deploy automatically through GitHub Actions.

## Deployment Configuration

The deployment is managed through GitHub Actions workflows defined in the repository. This means you don't need to run any local deployment commands like `hexo deploy`.

## Deployment Process

1. **Create or edit content** in your local repository
2. **Commit changes** using git commands
3. **Push to GitHub**: `git push origin main`
4. **GitHub Actions** will automatically build and deploy your site

## Benefits of GitHub Actions Deployment

- No need for local npm or npx commands
- Consistent build environment independent of your local setup
- Automated deployment on every push to the main branch
- Build logs and error reporting available in the GitHub Actions console

After GitHub Actions completes the workflow, your site will be available at: https://adrianwangs.github.io/
